problem:
Consider the problem of testing $H_0: X \sim f_0$ against $H_1: X \sim f_1$ based on a sample of size 1, where
\[ f_0(x) = \begin{cases} 
1 & \text{if } 0 \leq x \leq 1 \\
0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases} \]
and
\[ f_1(x) = \begin{cases} 
2 - 2x & \text{if } 0 \leq x \leq 1 \\
0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases} \]
Find the probability of type 2 error of the most powerful test of size $\alpha = 0.1$.

